    "commit_message": "model-router: fix embed model name to match Ollama's canonical tag (FND-002)\n\nSelf-improvement finding FND-002: routing_policy's \"nomic-embed-text\" (bare,\nno tag) doesn't match \"nomic-embed-text:latest\" in Ollama's available-models\nlist, flagged every cycle. Checked call_log.jsonl before touching anything -\nembed calls were 0-failure already (Ollama resolves the bare name via its\nown implicit :latest), so this was a cosmetic string mismatch, not a real\nbug. Fixed anyway since it's a one-line change that permanently silences\na false-positive drift signal.\n\nVerified live: restarted model-router.service, /api/model/embed still\nreturns a real embedding vector, no error.\n\nThe other 2 findings from this cycle (FND-001 uncommitted-artifacts,\nFND-003 elevated latency) don't need code changes - FND-001 was already\nstale (working tree was clean by the time this was checked), FND-003's\n\"7.19s average\" is the real, expected cost of Gemini API round-trips for\nself-improvement-analyse specifically, not a router-wide slowdown.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01F1KgvHcPTh7uQNNPDtxRuj",
